  "lease_id_form": "<run_id>.<trial_id>, one metering proxy process and one lease per trial in one ledger; --new-run on each start closes a lease a killed trial left open; each finalized lease is closed with budget-ledger.ts close",
  "lease_assumption": "serial requests (k = 1): the ledger admits a request while settled + every open reservation + the new reservation fits the lease, so two concurrent requests near R_max refuse each other with settled near zero; a 402 that overlapped an in-flight request (ledger created_at/settled_at) is infra:reservation_refused, never ceiling:lease; a reservation charged in full for an upstream failure is usd_charged_reservation on the row, outside the $1.00 bar and inside the cap",
  "dispatch": "by image id: each trial runs the manifest's recorded image id (docker image inspect .Id), checked against the tag again before the trial; a moved tag writes the trial as infra_error and stops the run with exit 2",
  "panel_cap_usd": 19,
  "stop_rule": "before each lease, from the ledger: settled + open reservations (an undrained request at its reserved value) + lease_usd <= panel_cap_usd, else the remaining rows are not_run:panel_cap and the run stops; a 402 after a forwarded request ends that trial as ceiling:lease (the trial failed the $1.00 bar) and the run continues; a proxy that does not start, a slot that does not bind, a cap check or lease close that fails, or an image id that moved writes that trial as infra_error (or its row with a note), the remaining rows as not_run:infra_stop, and the run stops; every planned trial has a row; no trial is ever replaced; the enforced worst case is the cap",
